# Playwright's JSON reporter output (playwright.config.ts). Two names are used:
# `results-gating.json` and, via PLAYWRIGHT_JSON_OUTPUT_NAME, `results-informational.json`.
# Anyone who runs the harness locally — even a bare `--list` — leaves one behind.
#
# Not merely untidy: a real run's report carries test titles, error messages and any
# interpolated URL, and this suite talks to STAGING. A committed report is a small
# disclosure surface. It also blocked a push here, via a `git status -- e2e/` guard.
#
# Infra, core#1197 — a second reason, and the sharper one. `results-gating.json` is the name CI's
# flaky detector READS: `.github/workflows/staging.yml` runs `detect_flaky_gating.py
# results-gating.json` with `if: always()`, at a path relative to the checkout, and the detector
# has no freshness guard. So a committed local report is readable by CI on any run that fails
# BEFORE writing its own — not hypothetical: a `grepInvert` drop and a missing module each
# produced `Total: 0 tests in 0 files` on 2026-09-10, and a zero-test run writes no report and
# exits 0. That is core#1232's shape arriving by file rather than by workflow run.
results-*.json
